# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but every script in
# it runs under WSL, Git Bash, or on the Android device. Without this file,
# checkout rewrites shell scripts to CRLF and `bash` then fails on the
# shebang line - `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not a program.
#
# That is not hypothetical: docs/kbase-notes.md records having to work around
# exactly this on src/mesa/wsl-build*.sh with `tr -d '\r' | bash`.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else that is read by a POSIX tool rather than
# by a Windows one.
makefile   text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.cross    text eol=lf

# SPIR-V modules are binary; never let them near line-ending translation.
*.spv binary
